{"repositoryId":1349430122,"availability":"available","full":"mikelninh/public-service-passport","name":"public-service-passport","description":"A citizen-first public service passport for safer benefit checks, reusable evidence and agent-assisted application preparation.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-28T09:34:13Z","updated":"2026-08-28T13:30:53Z","license":"MIT","branch":"feat/benefit-bridge-webmcp","homepage":"https://public-service-passport.netlify.app/","topics":["ai-agents","civic-tech","digital-government","govtech","javascript","netlify","public-services","webmcp"],"demo":"https://public-service-passport.netlify.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T15:45:34.212Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T15:45:34.212Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T15:45:34.212Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-18T15:45:34.212Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A working Berlin pilot that helps families understand possible public benefits, see what is known vs. uncertain, prepare the right evidence, and create a reviewable application draft — while keeping the final decision with the person and the authority.","The Authority Workbench and 100-case pilot are explicitly synthetic proofs. They demonstrate verified facts → authority preflight → exception handling → decision → payment instruction → settlement → reconciliation, but do not connect to a real authority or bank.","Public services repeatedly ask people for the same facts: household, children, income, rent, evidence. Citizens then have to work out which benefit might apply, which document is needed where, and what is actually certain."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mikelninh/public-service-passport/blob/feat%2Fbenefit-bridge-webmcp/README.md","fingerprint":"493ad88aee17fea31ccc3dc23b3b90ec6e2065fac9c62bfd4e16d481b1f1b4b0","extractedAt":"2026-10-18T15:45:34.430Z"},"